
  The plan is written: [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/plans/2026-10-02-deploys-page.md[39m. I haven't committed it and haven't started
  implementing, as you asked.

  [1mApproach.[0m The page is built from the template's component library in [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m, the same way [38;5;153moverview.js[39m is.
  [38;5;153msrc/pages/services.js[39m builds its own table, dropdown, chips and escaping instead, and the plan says not to copy it.
  The library already has what the spec needs:
  - [38;5;153mdataTable[39m handles sorting, the sort links and arrows, and the empty slot.
  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m + [38;5;153mselectField[39m give the environment dropdown, keep the current sort, and reload the page through [38;5;153mharbor.js[39m.
  - [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m has the tones: [38;5;153mok[39m, [38;5;153mbad[39m, [38;5;153mwarn[39m and [38;5;153minfo[39m for green, red, amber and blue.
  - [38;5;153memptyState[39m and [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m cover the empty message and the header.

  So there are no edits to [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m and no new CSS.

  [1mTasks:[0m
  1. [1mPage renderer:[0m [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m plus 10 rendering tests. They cover the header, the columns, the default and
     both sorts, the chips, the duration format, the filter keeping the sort, sort links keeping the filter, the empty
     state, and the fallback for unknown query values.
  2. [1mRoute and nav:[0m add one [38;5;153m/deploys[39m entry to the server's routes, which gets the existing 503 page for free. Add the
     nav link after Services. Three server tests cover the route, the nav order and the 503.

  [1mChecked:[0m I applied the plan's code to a scratch copy of the repo. The tests fail first exactly as the plan says, and
  then all 32 pass.

  [1mChoices where the spec wasn't explicit:[0m
  - An unknown [38;5;153mdir[39m falls back to [38;5;153mdesc[39m. So [38;5;153m?sort=service[39m with no [38;5;153mdir[39m lists Z→A. Clicking the header always sends an
    explicit direction, so this only shows up with hand-typed URLs.
  - "All environments" is the option with an empty value ([38;5;153m?env=[39m), the same convention as the existing select test.
  - If the environment is "all" and there are no deploys at all, the page says "No deploys". The spec only covers the
    filtered case.
  - Started shows the raw ISO timestamp, as the Services page does for its deploy time.

